&= \sum_{k = 1}^{1728} \frac{1}{(1+\omega^k)(1+\omega^{3k})}
&= \sum_{k = 1}^{1728} \frac{1}{1+\omega^k}\cdot\frac{1}{1+\omega^{3k}} \\
&= \left(\sum_{k = 1}^{1728} \frac{1}{1+\omega^k}\right)\cdot\left(\sum_{k = 1}^{1728} \frac{1}{1+\omega^{3k}}\right)
\end{align*}

Note that $\omega + \omega^2 + \omega^3 + 1 = 0,$ since $\omega$ is a complex cube root of unity.
This implies $\omega^{-3} = -\omega^2 - \omega - 1.$
So,
\begin{align*}
\sum_{k = 1}^{1728} \frac{1}{1+\omega^k} &= \sum_{k = 1}^{1728} \frac{1}{1-\omega^{k-1}} \\
&= \sum_{k = 1}^{1728} \frac{\omega^{k-1}}{1-\omega^{k-1}}
= \sum_{j = 0}^{1727} \frac{\omega^j}{1-\omega^j}
= \frac{1}{2} + \sum_{j = 1}^{1727} \frac{\omega^j}{1-\omega^j} \\
&= \frac{1}{2} + \frac{1}{2} \sum_{j = 1}^{1727} \frac{1-\omega^j + \omega^j}{1-\omega^j}
