Let's observe that $\mathop{\text{lcm}}[m,10^{10}]$ and $\mathop{\text{lcm}}[8m,10^{10}] \;(= 4 \cdot \mathop{\text{lcm}}[m,10^{10}]) $ are both multiples of $10^{10}$. Therefore, both must be divisible by all powers of primes that divides $10^{10}$. Since $10^{10} = 2^{40}\cdot 5^{20}\cdot 10^{20}$, the prime powers required are $2^0, 2^1, \dots, 2^{40}$, $5^0$, $5^1, \dots, 5^{20}$, $10^0$, $10^1, \dots, 10^{20}$.

