Since $n$ is the smallest integer satisfying these conditions, consider the smallest number with prime factors appearing up to $\sqrt{n}$. Specifically, choose the smallest multiple of 2 ($>2$), the smallest multiple of 3 ($>3$) and no multiple of any prime greater than 5 until $\sqrt{n}$ ($>5$).

