             &\approx \frac{3 \times 32P_{32} + 0.25 \times 32P_{48}}{1152} \quad\text{Ignore the fractional part in the numerator for easier calculations}\\
             &\approx 3.0576P_{32} + 0.0528P_{48}
\end{align*}

Since we don't have the original prices, we can't find exact values for the final answers. However, the equality above shows that the new price for the 32-ounce size depends on both the original prices of the 32-ounce and 48-ounce sizes.

