\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{amsmath}

\begin{document}
\begin{center}
If $m = 2n$, then we can substitute $m$ in the equation $70 + m + n - 20 = 80$ with $2n$ to obtain:
\begin{align*}
70 + 2n + n - 20 &= 80 \\
71 + 3n &= 80
\end{align*}
Now, we need to find the value of $n$ that makes the equation true. To do this, we will isolate $n$:
\begin{align*}
71 + 3n &= 80 \\
3n &= 80 - 71 \\
3n &= 9
\end{align*}
Now we will divide by $3$ to find $n$:
\begin{align*}
n &= \frac{9}{3} \\
n &= 3
\end{align*}
So the value of $n$ is $n=\boxed{3}$.
\end{center}
\end{document}
```

