\end{align*}
Now we substitute the expressions we expanded and simplified in the original equation:
\begin{align*}
\boxed{ x^4 } - 3 \boxed{ x^3 } + 4 \boxed{ x^2 } + 11 \boxed{ x } - 9 &= \left( \boxed{ x^4 } - 3 \boxed{ x^3 } + 2\boxed{ x^3 } + 4\boxed{ x^2 } \right) + \boxed{x^3 } - 3\boxed{x^3 } + 2x + \boxed{ 11x } - 9 \\
&= \boxed{x^4 } + \boxed{ x^3 } + \boxed{4x^2 } + \boxed{11x } - 11\boxed{ x } - 9
\end{align*}
Now, comparing the $x^3$ and above, we can find $x^3$ in the dividend and divisor, and subtract to get the remainder:
\begin{align*}
\boxed{ x^3 }_{dividend} -\boxed{ x^3 }_{divisor} &=  x^3 - (-x^3) \\
&= 2x^3
\end{align*}
